# .trivyignore — suppressions for the BLOCKING Trivy scans: the filesystem and
# config scans in .github/workflows/ci.yml and the deploy security gate in
# .github/workflows/deploy-aws.yml (severity CRITICAL,HIGH, exit-code 1).
#
# Rules (security audit 2026-09-24 INF-11, plan item P0-16a; enforced by
# scripts/ci/check-trivyignore-hygiene.mjs):
#   - every entry is `<ID> exp:YYYY-MM-DD`. Trivy honours `exp:` itself: on that
#     date the suppression lapses and the finding fails the scan again until a
#     person re-reviews it. At most 180 days out.
#   - every entry names an owner: and a reason: in the comment block above it.
#   - a per-resource property (S3 public-access block, bucket encryption,
#     CloudTrail settings, ...) is never suppressed here for the whole tree; it
#     is fixed, or excepted on the resource with an inline `#trivy:ignore:<ID>`
#     and a reason (docs/evidence/W2/2026-09-24-trivy/ is the precedent).
#   - a dependency entry mirrors a row of docs/security/dependency-risk-ledger.json
#     (the single decision record, enforced for npm audit by
#     scripts/ci/check-dependency-risk.mjs) and expires with it.
#
# Removed 2026-09-25 (P0-16a), each verified against the tree at that date;
# evidence docs/evidence/D6/2026-09-24-p0/P0-16a/:
#   AVD-AWS-0086 / 0087 / 0091 / 0093 (S3 public access block): every bucket in
#     terraform/ (bootstrap tfstate, cloudfront frontend, compliance-evidence,
#     stack vault) has an aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block with all four flags
#     true. The tree-wide ignore only hid the next bucket without one.
#   AVD-AWS-0016 (CloudTrail log-file validation): the one trail,
#     aws_cloudtrail.part11_audit in terraform/modules/compliance-evidence, sets
#     enable_log_file_validation = true.
#   CVE-2026-45829 (chromadb): the pin is gone from every requirements file;
#     `git grep -i chromadb` finds nothing outside documents.
#   GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 (react-router RSC CSRF): react-router and
#     react-router-dom are no longer in package.json or package-lock.json.
#
# Removed 2026-09-26 (W2; evidence docs/evidence/W2/2026-09-26-trivy-inline-ignores/):
#   DS002 (image runs as root): it fired on one file, the vendored skill image
#     .claude/skills/gstack/.github/docker/Dockerfile.ci, which is never built
#     or deployed here. The config scans in ci.yml and deploy-aws.yml now skip
#     that file alone (`skip-files`), so a new Dockerfile running as root
#     anywhere else fails the scan again.

# owner: Security Engineering (dependency-risk-ledger.json rows
#   GHSA-w3rx-r6r6-pgpr / GHSA-5p2g-fcmc-qvqq; expires with the ledger, 2026-11-25)
# reason: image-size CVE-2025-71329 (zero-valued size DoS) and CVE-2025-71330
#   (ICNS DoS), vulnerable range <=2.0.2. The only installed copy is
#   image-size@1.2.1, pulled solely by pptxgenjs@4.0.1 ("image-size": "^1.2.1").
#   No fixed version exists (latest published is 2.0.2, still in range, and 2.x is
#   outside pptxgenjs's range), so neither a bump nor an override remediates it.
#   Disposition UNREACHABLE per the ledger: the production PPTX generator uses no
#   image-capable pptxgenjs API and the shipped pptxgenjs Node bundle never
#   imports image-size, proven on every push by
#   scripts/ci/check-pptx-image-reachability.mjs and the require.cache runtime
#   test. Trivy scans package-lock.json separately from npm audit, so this is
#   the ledger decision mirrored for Trivy's scanner, not a second authority.
#   Drop when image-size ships a fix >2.0.2 and pptxgenjs widens its range (or
#   pptxgenjs is replaced). Re-check with `npm ls image-size --all`.
CVE-2025-71329 exp:2026-11-25
CVE-2025-71330 exp:2026-11-25
